PRAYER:
In the premises aforesaid, it is respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:
(a) Grant an ad-interim ex-parte temporary injunction restraining the Defendant, their agents, servants, assigns, and representatives from alienating, selling, transferring, encumbering, or creating third-party rights in respect of the suit schedule property during the pendency of the present suit;
(b) Restrain the Defendant from altering the nature or character of the suit schedule property;
(c) Pass such other or further relief(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances of the case.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, in light of the facts and circumstances stated above, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Direct that in the event of arrest of the Applicant in connection with FIR No. [NUMBER]/[YEAR] registered at Police Station [STATION] for offences under Sections [SECTIONS], the Applicant be released on anticipatory bail on such terms and conditions as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper;
(b) Grant ad-interim ex-parte protection from arrest to the Applicant during the pendency of the present application;
(c) Pass such other or further order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem just and equitable in the circumstances of the case.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, in the premises aforesaid, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble High Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Quash and set aside FIR No. [NUMBER]/[YEAR] dated [DATE], registered at Police Station [STATION], for offences punishable under Sections [SECTIONS], and all consequential proceedings arising therefrom, including the charge-sheet and summoning order;
(b) Stay further investigation/trial proceedings in the said FIR during the pendency of the present petition;
(c) Pass any other order(s) that this Hon'ble Court may deem fit, just, and proper in the interest of justice.

PRAYER:
It is therefore most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Pass an ex-parte ad-interim temporary injunction restraining the Defendant, their agents, servants, and representatives from alienating, selling, transferring, creating third-party rights, or changing the nature of the suit schedule property, during the pendency of the suit;
(b) Confirm the said interim injunction after hearing both parties upon notice;
(c) Award costs of the application to the Plaintiff.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, in light of the facts and circumstances stated above, the Petitioner most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble High Court may be pleased to:
(a) Issue a Writ of Mandamus or any other appropriate writ, order, or direction commanding the Respondent Authorities to consider and decide the Petitioner's statutory representation dated [DATE] in accordance with law within a stipulated timeframe;
(b) Direct the Respondent to disburse the lawful pensionary benefits and gratuity dues to the Petitioner along with statutory interest @ 9% per annum from the date of entitlement till actual realization;
(c) Award the costs of the petition to the Petitioner.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, in light of the facts and grounds stated above, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble High Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Call for the lower court records of Criminal Appeal/Case No. [NUMBER] from the Court of learned [JUDGE/COURT];
(b) Set aside and quash the impugned order/judgment dated [DATE] passed by the learned [COURT] in [CASE DETAILS];
(c) Acquit the Revisionist / discharge the Revisionist of all charges framed against them;
(d) Stay the operation of the impugned order/sentence during the pendency of the present Criminal Revision Petition;
(e) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the interest of justice.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, the Plaintiff most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to pass a judgment and decree:
(a) Directing the Defendant to specifically perform the Agreement to Sell dated [DATE] by receiving the balance sale consideration of Rs. [AMOUNT]/- and executing and registering the Sale Deed in favour of the Plaintiff in respect of the suit schedule property;
(b) In default of the Defendant doing so, direct an Officer of this Hon'ble Court to execute and register the Sale Deed on behalf of the Defendant;
(c) Direct delivery of vacant, peaceful physical possession of the suit property to the Plaintiff;
(d) In the alternative, direct refund of the earnest money of Rs. [AMOUNT]/- along with interest @ 18% per annum from the date of payment till realization;
(e) Award costs of the suit to the Plaintiff.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Rent Controller may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Pass an order of eviction in favour of the Petitioner/Landlord and against the Respondent/Tenant, directing the Respondent to vacate and hand over peaceful, vacant possession of the tenanted premises described in Schedule 'A' to the Petitioner on grounds of bona fide commercial/residential requirement;
(b) Direct the Respondent to pay arrears of rent and mesne profits amounting to Rs. [AMOUNT]/- till date of actual delivery of possession;
(c) Award costs of the eviction proceedings to the Petitioner.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, in light of the mutual consent and settlement arrived at between the parties, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Pass a decree of divorce by mutual consent under Section 13B(2) of the Hindu Marriage Act, 1955 dissolving the marriage solemnized between Petitioner No. 1 and Petitioner No. 2 on [DATE];
(b) Record full and final settlement of all claims regarding permanent alimony, maintenance, stridhan, and custody as per the Settlement Agreement dated [DATE];
(c) Pass any other order(s) that this Hon'ble Court may deem just and proper.

PRAYER:
It is therefore most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Condone the delay of [NUMBER] days in preferring the accompanying Appeal/Application against the impugned judgment/order dated [DATE] passed in [CASE DETAILS], in the interest of justice and on the sufficient grounds stated in the application;
(b) Direct the accompanying Appeal/Application to be taken on record and heard on merits;
(c) Pass such other or further order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances of the case.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Appellate Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Stay the operation and execution of the impugned judgment and decree dated [DATE] passed by the learned Trial Court in Original Suit No. [NUMBER] of 20[YEAR], during the pendency and final disposal of the present First Appeal;
(b) Restrain the Respondent from executing the decree or taking possession of the suit property in Execution Petition No. [NUMBER];
(c) Pass ex-parte ad-interim relief in terms of prayer (a) and (b);
(d) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, the Petitioner most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble High Court / Supreme Court may be pleased to:
(a) Exercise jurisdiction under Section 11(6) of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 and appoint an independent and impartial Sole Arbitrator to adjudicate all disputes and claims arising out of Contract/Agreement dated [DATE] between the Petitioner and Respondent;
(b) Direct that the arbitration shall be conducted under the aegis and rules of the High Court Arbitration Centre;
(c) Award costs of the present application to the Petitioner.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, in light of the facts and circumstances stated hereinabove, the Petitioner most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble High Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Issue a Writ of Habeas Corpus or any other appropriate writ, order, or direction commanding Respondent Nos. 1 to 3 to produce the corpus of the Petitioner's minor daughter / relative, [NAME], before this Hon'ble Court from the illegal and unlawful custody of Respondent No. 4;
(b) Direct that the said detenue be set at liberty and restored to the lawful custody and care of the Petitioner;
(c) Pass such other or further order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the interest of justice.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Grant an ex-parte ad-interim order restraining the Respondent, its directors, and agents from encashing or invoking Bank Guarantee No. [NUMBER] dated [DATE] for Rs. [AMOUNT]/- issued by [BANK NAME];
(b) Direct the Respondent to maintain status quo with respect to the project assets and contract site described in Schedule 'A';
(c) Direct the Respondent to deposit the disputed amount of Rs. [AMOUNT]/- in an interest-bearing escrow account pending constitution of the Arbitral Tribunal;
(d) Award costs of the application to the Petitioner.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, the Complainant most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble District Commission may graciously be pleased to direct the Opposite Party to:
(a) Refund the sum of Rs. [AMOUNT]/- paid by the Complainant towards purchase of the defective product / deficient services, along with interest @ 12% per annum from the date of payment till realization;
(b) Pay a sum of Rs. 1,00,000/- (Rupees One Lakh only) towards compensation for mental agony, harassment, and severe inconvenience caused to the Complainant;
(c) Pay a sum of Rs. 25,000/- towards litigation expenses to the Complainant;
(d) Pass any other relief that this Hon'ble Commission may deem fit.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, the Aggrieved Person/Applicant most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Pass a Protection Order under Section 18 of the PWDVA prohibiting the Respondents from committing any acts of domestic violence or entering the workplace of the Applicant;
(b) Pass a Residence Order under Section 19 restraining the Respondents from dispossessing the Applicant from the shared household;
(c) Direct the Respondent No. 1 to pay monetary relief and maintenance of Rs. [AMOUNT]/- per month under Section 20 for food, medical expenses, and child support;
(d) Direct Respondent No. 1 to pay compensation of Rs. [AMOUNT]/- under Section 22 for mental torture and emotional distress.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Direct the Accused to pay 20% of the cheque amount, amounting to Rs. [AMOUNT]/- (Rupees [WORDS] only), as interim compensation to the Complainant under Section 143A of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881;
(b) Direct that the said interim compensation be deposited or paid within sixty (60) days from the date of this order in terms of Section 143A(3) of the Act;
(c) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the interest of justice.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, in light of the mutual amicable settlement and Memorandum of Understanding dated [DATE] executed between the parties, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble High Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Exercise inherent powers under Section 482 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 and quash FIR No. [NUMBER]/[YEAR] registered at Police Station [STATION] under Sections [SECTIONS], and all consequential proceedings emanating therefrom against the Petitioners;
(b) Relieve the Petitioners of the agony of facing prolonged criminal trial in view of the personal and matrimonial compromise;
(c) Pass such other or further order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem just and equitable.

PRAYER:
It is therefore most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Dispense with the personal appearance of the Accused/Applicant before this Hon'ble Court under Section 205 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 on all routine dates of hearing, and permit the Applicant to be represented through their duly appointed counsel;
(b) The Applicant undertakes to appear in person whenever specifically directed by this Hon'ble Court for framing of charges or examination under Section 313 CrPC;
(c) Pass any further order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, in the premises aforesaid, the Petitioner most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble High Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Issue a Writ of Certiorari or any other appropriate writ, order, or direction calling for the original records of the impugned order dated [DATE] passed by Respondent No. [NUMBER] in [CASE DETAILS], and quash and set aside the same as being illegal, arbitrary, ultra vires, and in violation of natural justice;
(b) Direct the Respondent to restore the status quo ante and reinstate the Petitioner to their post with all consequential seniority and financial benefits;
(c) Award costs of the petition to the Petitioner.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, the Petitioner most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:
(a) Set aside and quash the Arbitral Award dated [DATE] passed by the learned Sole Arbitrator in Arbitration Case No. [NUMBER] under Section 34 of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 on grounds of patent illegality, conflict with public policy of India, and perversity of findings;
(b) Stay the execution and enforcement of the impugned arbitral award pending hearing of the present petition;
(c) Award costs of the petition to the Petitioner.
